      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Altogether 70 patients suffering from CHD with attacks of angina of effort received propranolol and syndnopharm therapy in an outpatient clinic. After therapy a positive clinical effect was noted in 83.6% of the patients, a positive ECG time course in 64.2%. The combined use of both drugs increased their efficacy. The combination was justified in case of nitrate intolerance and the absence of marked heart failure."},
